	 *
	 * Each sub-layer is a FIXED gradient painted once (position + colour never change). home-cinema.js drives
	 * only each layer's `opacity` and `transform: translate3d()` from scroll position, every frame, so the
	 * light flows continuously and is ALWAYS exactly where the camera is (the root fix for D-39's discrete,
	 * early-firing scene light). Because only opacity/transform change, there is NO per-frame gradient repaint:
	 * pure compositor work, CLS-safe. Each layer is centred at 50% 50% so JS can slide the pool anywhere by a
	 * single translate (e.g. the cool pool left + warm pool right = the specialisaties two-disciplines split,
